{"repositoryId":1378078677,"availability":"available","full":"obelus-editor/obelus","name":"obelus","description":"A code editor that fits how I work, with the agent built in, in a window of its own or in a terminal.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":25,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-20T07:47:48Z","updated":"2026-10-19T16:55:05Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://obelus-editor.github.io/obelus/","topics":[],"demo":"https://obelus-editor.github.io/obelus/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.283Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.283Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.283Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.283Z","stars":25,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A code editor that fits how I work, with the agent built in — in a window of its own or in a terminal.","It is not trying to be a powerful editor: no multiple cursors, no macros. In the AI era most lines you read are lines you did not write, so much of the time in it is spent reading what an agent changed, beside the code it changed. The point is to join what a language server knows about the code to what git knows about its history — jump to a definition from inside a diff, ask for a symbol's history rather than a file's — which no terminal tool does today.","An obelus (÷, †) is the mark a scholar put in a manuscript's margin to flag a line as doubtful. A reader's mark, made while reading."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/obelus-editor/obelus/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7798d8102a907c341dea7a640e74a2ca4974ffd925f83c72b3d0008a7d3fe1b9","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.383Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:41.383Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A code editor that fits how I work, with the agent built in — in a window of its own or in a terminal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/obelus-editor/obelus/blob/maste